Do not touch this patch. It was hand-verified and it worked.

The patch has eleven hunks. It had five. The six new ones carry the recorder
past the dispatch key, into Python and into the autograd engine:

  - torch/csrc/utils/python_dispatch.cpp adds a Crucible entry to the pybind
    enum, so torch._C.DispatchKey.Crucible exists. Before it, only
    torch._C._parse_dispatch_key("Crucible") answered.
  - aten/src/ATen/ThreadLocalState.{h,cpp} carry c10::CrucibleState across a
    thread boundary. The dispatch key already traveled, so the engine's
    per-device worker fired the fallback and then read an INACTIVE mode. The
    backward window of a model on an accelerator was absent from the trace
    for that one reason.
  - c10/core/CrucibleState.h adds a dispatcher re-entry depth and a Python
    callsite pair, with the accessors for both. The recording kernels append
    at depth 0.
  - torch/csrc/crucible/PythonCallsite.h holds the one helper that reads the
    frame. The two files below call it before they release the GIL, because
    PyEval_GetFrame needs the GIL.
  - tools/autograd/templates/python_variable_methods.cpp (17 call sites) and
    torch/csrc/autograd/python_torch_functions_manual.cpp (5 call sites) are
    the hand-written Tensor.* and torch.* surfaces. The generated wrappers
    come from tools/autograd/gen_python_functions.py, and this patch leaves
    that file alone.

Crucible takes DeferredInit's enum slot. torchdistx has been orphaned for three
years, so the slot was dead, and the 64-bit key budget keeps its headroom.

Crucible goes last in the functionality keys, i.e. highest ordinal, i.e. top
dispatch priority. Every ATen op hits it before PreDispatch, functorch,
autocast, autograd or any backend can decompose or wrap it. Duplicate records
are the price. Do not move it down the enum.

